      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "OK, critical analysis:\n\n**Opponent's board**: Inti (2/2, summoning sick), Greasewrench Goblin (3/2, +1/+1 counter), Marauding Mako (2/2, +1/+1 counter). Bloodghast in graveyard (comes back when they play a land!). 2 Blood Crypts (both tapped).\n\n**My board**: Swamp, Gloomlake Verge, Watery Grave (all untapped). 3 lands, 11 life.\n\n**My hand**: Restless Reef, Winternight Stories, Bitter Triumph, Insatiable Avarice, Harvester of Misery (5/4), Gloomlake Verge, Watery Grave, Intimidation Tactics.\n\nThis is urgent. They're going to attack with 3 creatures next turn (Inti + Goblin + Mako = 2+3+2 = 7 damage minimum, plus Inti's discard could add a counter and trample). That puts me at 4 or less!\n\n**Priority 1**: I need to play Harvester of Misery. It costs {3}{B}{B}. I have 3 lands. If I play a 4th land, I still only have 4. I need 5 mana. I can't cast it this turn.\n\n**Plan**: Play a land (Watery Grave untapped, shock to 9 life... or Gloomlake Verge which enters untapped for free if I control a Swamp or Island — I control a Swamp!). Let me check Gloomlake Verge:",
